    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d123-a13">

                <pb facs="0310" n="238" sameAs="frus:frus1882/pg238"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[lnclosure 12 in No. 349.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Lowell to Mr. Barrows</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1882-04-26"><hi rendition="#italic">April</hi> 26,
                        1882</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">Confidential.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have to acknowledge the reception of your
                    two letters of yesterday with accompanying papers.</p>
                <p>You will understand, of course, that the money offer I instructed you to make was
                    not intended as an inducement for the prisoner to leave Ireland, but simply as a
                    provision for his expenses to America in case he should be released by the
                    government here.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>J. R. LOWELL.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
